config MTK_CCCI_MD
	tristate "MediaTek MT6895 CCCI / modem bring-up"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on PM
	depends on REGULATOR
	help
	  Minimal mainline driver for the MediaTek CCCI / modem (MD) block on
	  MT6895 (Dimensity 8100).  It brings up the modem rails and the MD
	  power domain, releases the modem CPU from reset through the stock
	  ATF SIP call, reads the LK boot tag table out of the reserved
	  ccci_tag_mem region and then polls CCIF0 for the first handshake.

	  The modem firmware itself is loaded by the bootloader (LK), not by
	  this driver.

	  Say M here if you want to bring up the cellular modem on such a
	  device.  If unsure, say N.
